The [[Merchandise:Thu'um Master Blazer|Thu'um Master Blazer]] is a blazer by BlackMilk Clothing released on April 6(GMT)/7(AEST), 2026.{{ref|name=Lookbook|[https://blackmilkclothing.com/pages/the-elder-scrolls-lookbook "The Elder Scrolls Lookbook"], BlackMilk Clothing. March 31, 2026}}

It is long-sleeved and navy blue with the Imperial Dragon logo in the pocket position and the first two lines of the Song of the Dragonborn written in the [[Lore:Dragon Alphabet|Dragon Alphabet]] around the wrists, and the interior lining has a blue and black galaxy pattern with more Dragon writing; this consists of words of [[Skyrim:Dragon Shouts|Dragon Shouts]] including Soul Tear, Ice Form, and Whirlwind Sprint. 
{{NewLeft}}

==Description==
:'''''This blazer is obtained by learning twenty shouts.'''''<br>

:''The Thu'um Master Blazer takes its cues from the moment the Dragonborn finishes learning all twenty shouts. No more collecting Words. No more proving strength. Just control. The emblem at the chest reflects that mastery, its unreadable runes marking knowledge fully absorbed, not spoken aloud.''<br>

:''This structured blazer holds its shape like a disciplined breath. This isn't armour. It's what you wear when the Voice is already yours and you don't need to raise it. Dragonborn, Dragonborn, by his honour is sworn.'' 

:'''''Why You'll Love It <3:'''''

:* ''A sharp tailored collar that feels ceremonial, like standing before a Word Wall''
:* ''Structured and fully lined so it holds its form, no matter how powerful the shout''
:* ''Sleeve cuffs embroidered with dragon language reading, "Dovahkiin, Dovahkiin, naal ok zin los vahriin"''
:* ''Chest emblem worn like a quiet record of mastery, earned not given''
:* ''Functional pockets because even Thu'um Masters need somewhere to rest their hands''

==Material==
* Main: 65% Polyester, 31% Viscose, 4% Elastane
* Lining: 100% Polyester

